## State Machine Diagram

```mermaid
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Refraction_Active: mode = refraction
    Refraction_Active --> Layered_Fallback: moving = true (at once)
    Layered_Fallback --> Refraction_Recovering: moving = false
    Refraction_Recovering --> Layered_Fallback: Motion during the recovery
    Refraction_Recovering --> Refraction_Active: After 287ms (the rim fades back 60 + 220ms later)
    [*] --> Blur_Glass_Active: mode = blur or glass
    Blur_Glass_Active --> Fallback_Mode: moving = true (switches to fallbackMode at once)
    Fallback_Mode --> Settling: moving = false
    Settling --> Blur_Glass_Active: After 299ms
```
So a moving surface never drags a misaligned backdrop along, and it returns to full refraction once it stops.
